707,"t":"contest_end","x":"1707: Ajit Singh takes Jodhpur.","cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","c":3},{"y":1707,"t":"gain","x":"1707: Jodhpur is Ajit Singh's.","cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","c":3},{"y":1708,"t":"loss","x":"1708: Bahadur Shah takes control of Marwar.","m":2,"cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","c":3},{"y":1710,"t":"gain","x":"1710: Bahadur Shah recognises Ajit Singh.","cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","c":3},{"y":1818,"t":"vassal_start","x":"6 January 1818: Man Singh accepts the British alliance.","m":1,"cp":"british-empire","cpn":"British Empire in India (East India Company rule)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","c":3},{"y":1947,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1947: British suzerainty ends as Jodhpur accedes.","cp":"british-empire","cpn":"British Empire in India (East India Company rule)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","c":2},{"y":1949,"t":"dissolve","x":"1949: Jodhpur accedes to India.","cp":"republic-of-india","cpn":"Republic of India","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","c":2}],"wars":[{"name":"Mewar and Marwar over Mandore","from":1438,"to":1453,"outcome":"Ranmal was killed in 1438 by Kumbha's party; Mandore passed to Mewar until Jodha retook it in 1453.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Kumbha"},{"name":"Maldeo's conquests","from":1534,"to":1542,"outcome":"Maldeo took Nagaur and Ajmer (1534), Jalore (1538), Tonk and Toda (1539) and Bikaner (1542).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maldeo_Rathore"},{"name":"Sher Shah's occupation of Marwar","from":1544,"to":1545,"outcome":"Khawas Khan Marwat and Isa Khan Niyazi occupied Marwar in 1544; Maldeo regained it in 1545.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maldeo_Rathore"},{"name":"Battle of Harmoda","from":1557,"to":1557,"outcome":"Maldeo and Haji Khan defeated Udai Singh of Mewar in January 1557; Maldeo took Merta.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maldeo_Rathore"},{"name":"Akbar's conquest of Marwar","from":1557,"to":1583,"outcome":"The Mughals took Ajmer and Nagaur (1557), occupied Jaitaran (1558) and Jodhpur (1563-64), and dislodged Chandrasen from Bhadrajun (1570-71); Udai Singh was recognised as a Mughal ruler in 1583.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom"},{"name":"Mughal-Rathore war","from":1679,"to":1710,"outcome":"Aurangzeb took Marwar in 1678-79; Durgadas recaptured much of it in 1681-1687; Ajit Singh took Jodhpur in 1707-08; Bahadur Shah recognised him in 1710.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom"},{"name":"Maratha-Jodhpur wars","from":1787,"to":1791,"outcome":"Scindia's Marathas fought Jodhpur with defeats at Patan and Mertia in 1790; the page gives no border change.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom"}],"certainty":[{"from":1243,"to":1949,"level":"soft","note":"No survey or treaty line is on the pages opened; the subsidiary alliance of 6 January 1818 names no boundary."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","title":"Marwar Kingdom"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maldeo_Rathore","title":"Maldeo Rathore"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Kumbha","title":"Rana Kumbha"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rao_Sheoji","title":"Rao Sheoji"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bikaner_State","title":"Bikaner State"}]}